text:
**C1: confirmed.** At `src/documents.ts:19` the filter is `!doc.private || !canEdit(user, doc)`. This keeps a private document only when the user *cannot* edit it, which is the opposite of what the doc comment on line 17 promises. Ordinary users get the titles of other people's private documents, and owners and admins lose sight of their own. This leaks data and must be fixed before merge.

**C2: confirmed.** No `*.test.ts` or `*.spec.ts` files exist anywhere in the repo, so `visibleDocuments` and `listTitles` are untested. The repo has no test setup at all, so adding tests here is a suggestion, not a rule this change breaks. It is still worth doing, since a single test would have caught C1.

